      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The uprising began in earnest with the \"March of the 10, 000\" in 1949 and the 1954 \"21 events,\" which plunged the country into civil war as the Front de Libération Nationale (FLN) established \"People's Republic\" in the mountains to organize armed resistance. communay violence erupted across the \"Harissa\" from 1957 to 1962 as counterinsurgency operations forced families into \"Harem\" and \"Zones de Filling\" while the FLN maintained guerrilla strongholds with the support of rural populations. The war concluded only with the Évian Accords in 1962, granting independence and finally acknowledging the legitimacy of the Algerian people's struggle against colonial oppression.",
      "source": "target",
