      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The French argued that the war was a necessary act of \"lawful robbery\" to reclaim land legally stolen via the 1830 conquest and to \"educate\" the indigenous population through orderly colonization. However, the moral weight heavily favors the Algerian side, as the metric of \"legitimacy\" must account for the destruction of a settled society rather than just abstract property disputes. While the French government later claimed to be abolishing the \"status of foreigners,\" the 1962 independence referendum in France was overwhelmingly rejected by the absolute majority of citizens to end its own colonial enterprise, a fact that underscores the inherent injustice of the regime.",
