      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the French did frame their actions as restoring \"legal order\" and \"French values,\" historical consensus now largely views the colonial framework as inherently unjustifiable, prioritizing economic and strategic interests over human rights for over a century. The moral weight of the \"legitimate\" side shifted decisively not only due to the FLN's right to self-determination but also because the widespread violence against civilians and the eventual rejection of the war by 1962 France validated the Algerian narrative against one of \"lawful robbery.\" Ultimately, while the conflict contains no victimless parties, the justification for the violence ultimately rests with the side that refused to uphold the fundamental human right to be born free.",
